## Building a Game Character

A character has a name, current HP, and maximum HP. Damage reduces HP; healing restores it — but HP must stay between 0 and `max_hp`.

### The Character Struct

```xiom
type Character = {
  name: Str;
  hp: Int;
  max_hp: Int;
}
```

### Taking Damage

Subtract damage, but don't go below 0:

```xiom
fn Character.take_damage(self, amount: Int) {
  hp = hp - amount;
  if hp < 0 {
    hp = 0;
  }
}
```

### Healing

Add HP, but clamp to `max_hp`:

```xiom
fn Character.heal(self, amount: Int) {
  hp = hp + amount;
  if hp > max_hp {
    hp = max_hp;
  }
}
```

### Putting It Together

```xiom
var hero = Character{ name: "Knight"; hp: 80; max_hp: 100; };

hero.take_damage(30);  // hp = 50
hero.take_damage(90);  // hp = 0 (clamped)
hero.heal(25);         // hp = 25
hero.heal(200);        // hp = 100 (clamped to max)
```

### Guard Conditions

The `if hp < 0` and `if hp > max_hp` checks are **guard conditions** — they prevent the HP from ever entering an invalid range. This is called **clamping**.

